<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 14.0 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 14.0 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected on average to issue 14.0 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT) at its mid-month auction on February 11 against 16.5 trillion lire worth maturing, a Reuter poll of analysts showed.</p>
<p>Forecasts range from 13.5 to 15.75 trillion lire of BOTs.</p>
<p>Zero coupon certificates (CTZ) for some 10 trillion lire will be maturing for the first time at the end of February.</p>
<p>The Treasury is expected to issue 2.0 trillion lire of 18-month CTZ and 2.5 trillion lire of two-year CTZ, according to the analysts' consensus.</p>
<p>Settlement date for the paper is February 14.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trillion of lire):</p>
<p>			   3mo  6mo  12mo  Tot BOT  18mo CTZ  2-yr CTZ</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Maturing	   3.5   6.0  7.0   16.5	--	 --</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Credito Italiano 3.0   5.0  5.5   13.5     2.0	 2.5</p>
<p>    Caboto	     3.0   5.0  6.0   14.0     2.0	 2.5</p>
<p>    Indosuez	   3.0   4.5  6.0   13.5     2.5	 2.5</p>
<p>    J.P. Morgan	3.0   5.0  6.0   14.0     2.0	 2.5</p>
<p>    Prometeia	  3.0   5.0  6.0   14.0	   8.0*</p>
<p>    Banca di Roma    2.5   5.0  6.5   14.0     1.5	 2.5</p>
<p>    BCI		  3.0   5.5  7.25  15.75    1.5	 2.5</p>
<p>============================================================</p>
<p>    Consensus	  3.0   5.0  6.0   14.0     2.0	 2.5</p>
<p>============================================================</p>
<p>* The forecast is for the entire month of February</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392 66129437</p>
</text>
